Create /Users/tarekmnif/kognai/workspace/tools/ia-scraper/src/ia-client.ts

Build a typed client for the Internet Archive search API (archive.org/advancedsearch.php).

Imports TopicConfig from ./viral-topics for the topic-aware search variant.

Exports:
```typescript
export interface IAItem {
  identifier: string;
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  mediatype: string;         // 'movies' | 'audio' | 'texts' | 'image'
  subject?: string[];        // tags/keywords
  creator?: string;
  date?: string;
  downloads?: number;
  views?: number;
  addeddate?: string;
  publicdate?: string;
  source_url: string;        // direct link: archive.org/details/{identifier}
  topic_id?: string;         // which TopicConfig.id sourced this item (set by caller)
}

export interface IASearchParams {
  query: string;
  mediatype?: 'movies' | 'audio' | 'texts' | 'image';
  collection?: string;       // optional: filter to specific IA collection (e.g. 'prelinger')
  sort?: 'downloads desc' | 'publicdate desc' | 'views desc';
  rows?: number;             // default 50, max 200
  page?: number;             // default 1
  date_from?: string;        // YYYY-MM-DD
  date_to?: string;          // YYYY-MM-DD
}

export interface IASearchResult {
  items: IAItem[];
  total: number;
  page: number;
  rows: number;
}

export async function searchInternetArchive(params: IASearchParams): Promise<IASearchResult>;
export async function searchByTopic(topic: TopicConfig, rows?: number): Promise<IAItem[]>;
export async function getItemMetadata(identifier: string): Promise<IAItem | null>;
```

searchByTopic: iterates topic.ia_queries, calls searchInternetArchive for each with topic.mediatype and topic.ia_collection, deduplicates by identifier, sets item.topic_id = topic.id on all results.

Implementation:
- Use fetch() — no external HTTP libraries
- API endpoint: https://archive.org/advancedsearch.php?q={query}&fl[]=identifier,title,description,mediatype,subject,creator,date,downloads,views,addeddate,publicdate&sort[]={sort}&rows={rows}&page={page}&output=json
- Add collection filter when set: &fq[]=collection:{collection}
- Handle rate limiting: 1 request/second max (add sleep helper)
- Handle errors gracefully: return empty result on 429/5xx, log warning
- Build source_url as `https://archive.org/details/{identifier}`
- Max 130 lines. TypeScript strict mode. JSDoc on all exports.

Create /Users/tarekmnif/kognai/workspace/tools/ia-scraper/src/runner.ts

The main entry point. Iterates VIRAL_TOPICS (from viral-topics.ts) to drive all IA searches, then scores and stores results.

Exports:
```typescript
export interface RunConfig {
  topics?: TopicConfig[];      // default: VIRAL_TOPICS (all 30)
  top_n_topics?: number;       // if set, only run TOP_N_TOPICS (e.g. 10)
  rows_per_query?: number;     // rows per IA query per topic (default 50)
  min_score?: number;          // only store items with score >= this (default 30)
  sprint_id: string;
  dry_run?: boolean;           // if true: log but don't write to Supabase
}

export interface TopicResult {
  topic_id: string;
  topic_name: string;
  items_fetched: number;
  items_stored: number;
  top_item?: ScoredItem;       // highest scoring item for this topic
}

export interface RunResult {
  topics_run: number;
  items_fetched: number;
  items_scored: number;
  items_stored: number;
  per_topic: TopicResult[];
  top_items: ScoredItem[];     // global top 5 by score across all topics
  errors: string[];
  duration_ms: number;
}

export async function runScraper(config: RunConfig): Promise<RunResult>;
```

Pipeline per topic:
1. Call searchByTopic(topic, rows_per_query) — returns IAItem[] with topic_id set
2. Score each item with scoreItem()
3. Filter: score >= (topic.min_score ?? config.min_score ?? 30)
4. If !dry_run: upsertItems(filtered, sprint_id)
5. Track per-topic stats in TopicResult

After all topics:
- Deduplicate across topics by identifier (keep highest score)
- Sort all stored items by score desc for global top 5
- Log final RunResult summary table

Entry point (when run directly):
```typescript
if (import.meta.url === `file://${process.argv[1]}`) {
  const config: RunConfig = {
    top_n_topics: process.argv.includes('--all') ? undefined : 10,
    sprint_id: 'sprint-052',
    dry_run: process.argv.includes('--dry-run'),
    min_score: 30,
  };
  runScraper(config).then(r => {
    console.log('\n=== RUN COMPLETE ===');
    console.log(`Topics: ${r.topics_run} | Fetched: ${r.items_fetched} | Stored: ${r.items_stored}`);
    console.log('Top 5:', r.top_items.map(i => `${i.title} (${i.score.toFixed(1)})`));
  });
}
```

